# Loaded by `vite --mode desktop`, which is the build Tauri packages.
#
# The desktop and mobile shells serve the game from tauri://localhost, so the
# same-origin path the web build uses (`/v1`) resolves to the app bundle and
# not to the API. A packaged build therefore needs an absolute API origin, and
# this is where it comes from.
#
# The default points at a server running on the same machine, which is what a
# developer has. Point it at the real deployment when building something to
# ship - either by editing this file, or by exporting VITE_API_URL before the
# build, which wins over anything written here:
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com npm run desktop:build
#
# Whatever origin is used must list the shells' own origins in the server's
# CORS_ORIGINS, because these requests are cross-origin:
#
#   CORS_ORIGINS=tauri://localhost,http://tauri.localhost
#
# With an absolute API origin the refresh token cannot travel as an httpOnly
# cookie (different site), so the client falls back to storing it - see
# `usesCookieSession` in src/core/account/session.ts.
VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787
